course: dictionary
lesson: 15555
title: Supine: lying on your back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe a position, which is how a body is lying or standing. «Lie supine on the mat, with your face looking up at the ceiling.» If you are lying on your back with your face up, you are supine.
explain: The opposite is prone, which means lying face down. Doctors, nurses and PE teachers use both words. If you can see the ceiling, you are supine. If you can only see the floor, you are prone.
explain: Supine can also describe people. «The council was supine and let the builders knock down the park without a word.» The council did not fight back, so supine here means weak and too willing to accept things without protesting.
explain: Clue words help you choose the right meaning. Lying on a mat or on a bed points to the first meaning. Doing nothing and letting things happen points to the second.
fact: Supine means lying flat on your back, face upwards.
fact: «Supine position» is a phrase used in science, PE and first-aid lessons.
fact: Prone is the opposite of supine: it means lying flat on your face.
fact: In formal writing, supine means weak, lazy or too willing to accept things without protesting.
fact: A «supine government» is one that does nothing when it should act.
exercise: «The nurse asked Sam to lie supine on the mat.» What does supine mean here? | Running around the room | Lying face down on his front | Standing up tall and straight | *Lying flat on his back, face up
exercise: «The council stayed supine and let the company cut down the trees without a word.» What does supine suggest? | Busy and very hardworking | *Weak and too willing to accept things without protest | Angry and shouting at everyone
exercise: Which word means lying face down, the opposite of supine? | *Prone | Standing | Supine
test: «The patient lay supine while the doctor checked her chest.» Where was the patient lying? | Sitting in a chair | Hanging from the ceiling | Face down on the bed | *Flat on her back, face up
test: «Our class was supine, so nobody complained when the fire drill was cancelled.» What does supine mean here? | Loud and angry | Very quick and clever | *Weak and too willing to accept things without protest | Shy and always hiding
exam: «After the fall, Ravi lay supine on the grass, looking up at the clouds.» What does supine mean here? | Running towards the clouds | Hiding under a tree | Lying on his front, face down | *Lying on his back, face up
